              "type": "text",
              "content": "Patterns in Life: Diversity and Classification"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.857,
            0.018,
            0.952,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "N 251"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.093,
            0.776,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vi) If classification were based only on habitat, which organisms might be incorrectly grouped together? Explain the scientific consequences of such a classification."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.144,
            0.776,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vii) Imagine scientists discover a new organism that is multicellular, eukaryotic, lacks chlorophyll and absorbs nutrients from a host externally. Should it be placed under fungi or animalia? Justify your reasoning using classification criteria."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.344,
            0.261,
            0.608,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Journey Beyond"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.322,
            0.775,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Visit a nearby park or a water body. Observe the water body and its surroundings. Identify ten organisms and classify them into kingdoms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.36,
            0.774,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Interview a gardener or a forest worker. Ask them how they identify species. Compare the traditional scientific methods of identification."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.397,
            0.775,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y If you were studying the Pakke Tiger Reserve or any other bird sanctuary of your choice, how would you organise the information about the bird species?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.451,
            0.776,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Conduct a survey in a forest area near a village, identify edible and poisonous mushrooms with the help of indigenous knowledge of community resource person(s)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.506,
            0.776,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Collect and study the postal stamps of India and the world released over time on diversified flora and fauna. Based on your learning, make your own criteria and classify them. Organise a philately (collection of postage stamps) exhibition in your school and showcase your work in this exhibition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.594,
            0.775,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Investigate an extinct species and analyse how its disappearance impacted the organisms that depend on it, and how this affected the ecological balance of the ecosystem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.813,
            0.39,
            0.956,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
